        "format": "Short Paper", 
        "archival": false,       
        "title": "Do Agents Do What Developers Say? Instruction-Following Accuracy as an Evaluation Framework",
        "subtitle": "Measuring how faithfully AI agents follow developer-authored instructions",
        "venue": "Microsoft MLADS+ Agents Conference",
        "date": "Nov 2025",
        "sortDate": "2025-11-01",
        "summary": "We introduce a way to measure whether an AI agent truly follows the instructions its developers gave it — not just what end-users ask it to do. This helps teams catch mistakes early, build more reliable AI systems, and make sure agents behave the way they were intended to.",
        // "abstract": "Paste the original technical abstract of the paper here to enable the toggle.",
        "tags": ["Agent Evaluation", "LLM", "Instruction Following"]
    },
    {
